</blockquote><p data-structure="Section" id="p_94">VALIDITY OF SECTION 49
The law relating to electricity is principally contained  in
two Acts.
</p><p data-structure="Section" id="p_95">(i)<a href="https://indiankanoon.org/doc/261195/" id="a_138">The	 Indian	 Electricity  Act</a>  of  1910   (hereinafter
referred  to  as the "<a href="https://indiankanoon.org/doc/177537342/" id="a_139">Electricity Act</a>").  'Ms  provides	 for
grant  of licences in relation to supply of electricity	 and
the  projects of undertakings.	It also provides for  supply
of electricity including the protective clauses.
</p><p data-structure="Section" id="p_96">(ii)<a href="https://indiankanoon.org/doc/701121/" id="a_140">The	 Electricity  (Supply)	Act</a>  of	 1948	(hereinafter
referred  to as the "<a href="https://indiankanoon.org/doc/701121/" id="a_141">Supply Act</a>") provides for	constitution
of State Electricity Boards, the powers and- duties of	such
Boards.	 Certain important
<span class="hidden_text" id="span_61">244</span>
provisions of the Act may now be seen.
</p><p data-structure="Section" id="p_97"><a href="https://indiankanoon.org/doc/358102/" id="a_142">Section 2</a> is interpretation Section,
